CAVEAT:  Both sessions were eBGP between three different private AS numbers; no iBGP
         session was configured, so nothing here establishes iBGP behaviour or the
         iBGP administrative distance. Each partner advertised exactly ONE prefix --
         well inside swi_b's Base-licence BGP-64 limit -- so prefix scale was not
         exercised. The address family measured is the one the OPEN negotiated, AFI
         IPv4 / SAFI Unicast. The whole BGP configuration applied is quoted in
         STEPS 3 and 9 -- `router bgp`, `bgp router-id`, `neighbor ... remote-as` and
         `network` -- so no routing policy of any kind (route-map, prefix-list,
         community) was exercised. One unresolved disagreement was
         measured and is recorded in STEP 9: `show running-config` renders
         ` bgp graceful-restart` on a freshly created instance while
         `copy running-config` writes ` no bgp graceful-restart` and the DUT's own
         OPEN advertises no Graceful Restart capability. Nothing in this case depends
         on graceful restart, and which of the two is intended was not established
         here. ICMP destination-unreachable generation is rate-limited on this
         platform, so where type 3 packets are quoted their SOURCE is the attribution
         and their COUNT is not a measurement.

