     on swi_b's loopback and 10.90.90.1 only on swi_a's -- so each reply proves the
     frame reached that specific partner and came back. The unrouted control, sent in
     the same 20-frame leg with the same next-hop MAC, got nothing, so the DUT is
     making a per-destination routing decision and not flooding; and the DUT carries
     no static route, so BGP is the only thing that can have put these routes there.

